    "content": "## I.LPRC — Report C \"Lead Disposition Detail\" (leads / funnel / source) (thin transport ONLY)\n\nGmail → POST raw PDF bytes → LP-MCP. ZERO parsing here. Cadence recommendation (2026-08-05): LP schedules a month-to-date pull daily ~6:30 ET + a monthly full-YTD validation pull; request CSV/XLS if LP's scheduler ever allows it — the CSVs carry cents, the PDFs round.\n\n**PARSER PENDING (fail-closed):** the LP-MCP endpoint `/n8n/admin/lp-report-ingest/lead-disposition` ARCHIVES the PDF, logs `parser_pending` in scorecard_ingest_log, alerts GroupMe, and writes NOTHING — no sample PDF of this report existed on 2026-08-05, so no parser is built yet. The first real email IS the sample: pin this `q` subject filter against it (TO-VERIFY — exact subject unknown; LP's own export spells the sibling report \"Anlysis\"), then build the parser in LP-MCP `src/jobs/`, then the endpoint goes live. The 2026-08-05 YTD backfill entered via CSV (`/n8n/admin/lp-csv-ingest/lead-disposition`).\n\nA 200 with success:false = deterministic rejection — do NOT retry. 5xx = transport error — node retries 3x."
